/.direnv
/.claude
/target

# Nix profile + GC root created by `just seed-cache` and by .woodpecker/test.yaml
# (`nix develop --profile ./.ci-profile`). Keeping it locally is deliberate — it
# pins the CI closure against garbage collection — but it must never be committed.
/.ci-profile
/.ci-profile-*-link

# GC root for the compiled dependency tree, created by .github/workflows/ci.yml
# so the Nix-store cache step cannot collect the one path worth caching.
/.ci-artifacts

# Local environment files (keep .env.example tracked)
.env
!.env.example

# Shell/editor/tooling dotfiles that agent sandboxes and IDEs drop into the repo
# root. These are home-directory files with no business being here, but they
# reappear on their own, so ignoring them keeps `git status` readable.
#
# All anchored with a leading `/` so they only match the repo root — a crate that
# legitimately ships one of these names is unaffected.
#
# `.gitmodules` is listed deliberately: this repo has no submodules (no gitlink
# entries in the index), so a `.gitmodules` appearing here is always spurious.
# Delete this line the day real submodules are added, or git will ignore config
# it needs.
/.bashrc
/.bash_profile
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.mcp.json
/.profile
/.ripgreprc
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
/.zsh_rc
# No trailing slash: the sandbox drops these as plain files, not directories, and
# a `/.idea/` pattern would only match a directory.
/.idea
/.vscode
